## RINGKASAN

Market Stage: Growth
Primary Category: Ethereum Layer 2 Scaling / Optimistic Rollup
Competitor Count: 8+ major L2 competitors (Arbitrum, Base, Polygon zkEVM/CDK, Linea, Scroll, Mantle, zkSync Era, Starknet)
Major Narrative: L2 Scaling, Modular Framework (OP Stack), Superchain/Interoperability, Public Goods Funding (RetroPGF)
Trading Availability: 10+ major CEXs (spot + perpetuals), 3+ major DEXs (Velodrome, Aerodrome, Uniswap), deep liquidity
Adoption Metrics Available: TVL, Daily Active Addresses, Transactions, Wallets, Developer Count, Bridge Volume, Token Holders, Market Cap, Trading Volume, Chain Count, RetroPGF Distribution

## Open Threads

- Exact current TVL for each OP Stack chain (Base, World Chain, Zora Network, Mode, Fraxtal, Lyra) — DefiLlama has individual pages but aggregate Superchain TVL not officially published
- Real-time daily active address count — Dune dashboards exist but vary by methodology; no single official source
- Monthly active developer count for OP Stack specifically vs. Optimism ecosystem — Electric Capital report aggregates but methodology not fully transparent
- Bridge volume breakdown by bridge (Standard Bridge vs Hop vs Across vs Synapse) — Dune has data but not official
- Exact OP token holder count including bridged representations on Ethereum L1, Base, other chains — Etherscan only shows OP Mainnet L2 holders
- Market share calculation methodology for "Superchain aggregate TVL #1" — not officially published by DefiLlama; requires manual aggregation
- Competitor chain count comparisons (Arbitrum Orbit, Polygon CDK, ZK Stack) — respective registries not always up to date or directly comparable (mainnet vs testnet counting)
- RetroPGF Round 4 exact OP amount — blog announces completion but no nominal disclosure
- Airdrop #5+ timeline and criteria — Foundation signals future airdrops but no published schedule
- Granite upgrade mainnet activation date — testnet only currently, no confirmed timeline
- Permissionless fault proof mainnet deployment — Stage 2 decentralization target not officially dated
- OP staking design for shared sequencing — ethresear.ch discussions but no formal spec
- Legal classification of OP token — Foundation maintains utility stance but no regulatory no-action letter
- Revenue figures (sequencer fees, bridge fees) — not publicly disclosed; Token Terminal estimates only
- Treasury composition and size — not transparent; governance proposals show spending but not total holdings